{"id": "EUVD-2026-81743", "enisaUuid": "59a461ce-bd63-33ce-946c-c3d09d277952", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npnfs/blocklayout: Fix device leaks on parse failure\n\nbl_parse_concat() and bl_parse_stripe() allocate a child device array and\nthen parse each child in turn.  If parsing a child fails, the failed child is\nnot counted in nr_children and the parent may be left with a children array\nthat bl_free_device() will not release when nr_children is zero.\n\nRelease the failed child and the already parsed children before returning the\nerror.  Also make bl_free_device() release the child array whenever the\nchildren pointer is set, so that partially initialised concat or stripe\ndevices are cleaned up correctly.\n\nbl_parse_scsi() can also fail after assigning d->bdev_file and dropping the\nfile reference.  Clear the pointer after fput() so that an outer cleanup path\ndoes not put it again.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51d162dfb618f6cf3aa5e331c0305e27771ad884", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a2494964edac2a13e82441c2bf887548dc3be0b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1e1c36b206c659cf94c6755a1d821ed1babd32bc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23e4162405c456ce12c772d5882d306135e828ae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c056f817e4200fb18079d5052c273a22f191ff0a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90150", "GHSA-qj3f-qfg4-pxhf"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "038c035a-1f3a-36e7-a1a3-ac0fc061b467", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5c83746a0cf2831d4b59f5cf99ef5fbf138564e4 <8a2494964edac2a13e82441c2bf887548dc3be0b"}, {"id": "13f49478-2dfc-3516-a568-2713591ea22c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "458bba2e-c370-322a-bb64-1db1194bdc88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8f58af47-c763-3a53-97e8-983bdef19846", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5c83746a0cf2831d4b59f5cf99ef5fbf138564e4 <51d162dfb618f6cf3aa5e331c0305e27771ad884"}, {"id": "9ee9eac4-9e74-3a65-916a-1a57766aa64b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9f3a6fa5-e935-3ee9-a527-bb5428465f61", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5c83746a0cf2831d4b59f5cf99ef5fbf138564e4 <1e1c36b206c659cf94c6755a1d821ed1babd32bc"}, {"id": "a1a190b2-4494-364d-80a5-4e06c9c3a153", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "b402fa6f-c2d2-3c07-a599-bd678a9c9f1e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.18"}, {"id": "bfc8012f-603e-3f4a-bfdf-caac27ebf419", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5c83746a0cf2831d4b59f5cf99ef5fbf138564e4 <c056f817e4200fb18079d5052c273a22f191ff0a"}, {"id": "c10e27ff-cadf-38c9-a226-e2dccf106a53", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "faefc4f6-4d71-36bb-b413-6c276544ab9c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5c83746a0cf2831d4b59f5cf99ef5fbf138564e4 <23e4162405c456ce12c772d5882d306135e828ae"}, {"id": "fbd7a393-1819-308d-b6d4-a24ce3dbe41c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "85716620-6f47-3d5a-8dfa-928c896c11c3", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}